    "hints": [
        "Let <code>x</code> be the XOR of all elements. Handle the cases where <code>x == 0</code> or all elements are equal first.",
        "Replacing <code>a</code> with <code>a ^ b</code> changes the total XOR by <code>b</code>. Consider the smallest subset of original elements whose XOR equals <code>x</code>.",
        "If this subset has size <code>d</code>, the answer is <code>d</code> when <code>d &lt; nums.length</code>, and -1 otherwise.",
        "Find <code>d</code> using BFS from XOR value 0. Each transition XORs the current value with a distinct value from <code>nums</code>. All reachable XOR values are less than 2048."
